# Docker build-context excludes. The repo root is the build context for every
# service image (`docker build ... .`); without this file Docker tars the whole
# tree — ~5.9G, dominated by `.claude/` session transcripts — and sends it to the
# daemon before any layer runs (slow; can stall a build mid-send).
#
# Scope: ONLY paths no Dockerfile ever COPYs — VCS, the local venv, tool caches,
# session transcripts, and the research data snapshot. Source dirs and
# node_modules are intentionally NOT excluded so apps/web/Dockerfile and the
# services/* images are unaffected.
.claude/
.git/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Research data snapshots + run outputs (hundreds of MB of LEAN bars; never built
# into an image — the harness mounts a copy at run time, design §4.2).
research/data/cache/
research/runs/
